schoolhouse:
To-day are tilled and cultivated lands;
The schoolhouse tow'rs where Bruin had his den,
And where the wigwam stood the chapel stands;

schoolboys:
Throwing his scanty clothes off for a swim;
And schoolboys, from Bridge-tunnel going home,
Watching the waters downward dash and foam.

scheme:
Are but so many seconds.  We agreed
That the next man who came should prove the scheme;
And you were he.  Jan handed you the crock.

schooners:
Of captive wind that moans for fields and seas;
Seas cooling warm where native schooners drift
Through sleepy waters, while gulls wheel and sweep,

schools:
